+      "body": "fix(setup): edit the duplicate JSON member that clients read (#4957)\n\nJSON.parse, JSONC parse, and native Claude Code keep the last duplicate\nobject member, and parseClientConfiguration therefore validates the last\none. The shared setup/uninstall serializer instead edited text through\njsonc-parser's modify and findNodeAtLocation, which select the first\nmatching member, so setup and uninstall on configurations with repeated\nserver tables or rea members wrote into a shadowed member and failed\nreadback.\n\nLocate every JSON text edit by the effective (last) member in one place,\nreplacing the first-member modify path. Removing an effective member\nthat shadows an earlier duplicate would activate that duplicate, whatever\nits ownership, so the serializer now returns a tagged shadowed_member\nfailure and setup and uninstall refuse before writing a backup or the\nconfiguration.\n\nFixes #4952\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
